# ─── Secrets & environment files — NEVER commit these ────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.prod
.env.prod.*
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.prod
frontend/.env
llm-service/.env
# Catch-all: ignore EVERY dotenv variant (.env.aztest, .env.dev, .env.staging,
# …) so a newly-created environment file can never be committed by accident.
# The earlier explicit lines only covered .env/.env.local/.env.prod; a file like
# .env.aztest slipped through. The !…example negations below keep the tracked
# templates visible.
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
!.env*.example
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.prod.example
!**/.env*.example

# ─── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/

# ─── Build outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
dist/
build/
bin/
api-gateway/server

# ─── Language artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.py[cod]
*.test
*.out
debug
.gocache/

# ─── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.cursor/

# ─── Project-specific ignores ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchored to repo root: ignores a locally-cloned SigNoz runtime at /signoz/,
# but NOT deploy/signoz/ (our committed dashboard + alert + README assets).
/signoz/
!deploy/signoz/
logs/
# docs/ is tracked in git — remove this line if you want to untrack it
# docs/
.promotion.lock
**/.promotion.lock
**/.tmp/
**/_toolcache/
.cursor_tmp_*.log
e2e_run_output.txt
backend-orchestrator/agent-logs/
backend-orchestrator/backend-orchestrator/
artifacts/
artifacts_debug/
test-results/

# Local dev compose override — auto-loaded by `docker compose up`; keep it LOCAL
# so personal ports/CORS origins never leak into everyone's stack. Copy
# docker-compose.override.yml.example to start one.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Compiled Go binaries (no extension, named after dir)
api-gateway/api-gateway
backend-orchestrator/backend-orchestrator
backend-temporal-adapter/adapter
# kafka-mcp-sink Go worker — built from source by the Dockerfile (worker-builder
# stage), so the binary must never be committed. The image overrides any checked-in
# copy; committed copies are pure dead weight (~47MB) and look authoritative.
# NOTE: the broad `**/kafka-sink-worker` glob also matched the SOURCE package dir
# `worker-src/cmd/kafka-sink-worker/`, so git refused to descend into it and any
# NEW .go file there was silently ignored (main.go only survived via `git add -f`).
# That is a prod-correctness hazard: the sink is the CDC write path, so a dropped
# source file means the image builds from stale code. Fix: re-include the source
# package dir explicitly; the binary (built to worker-src/kafka-sink-worker and any
# stray dev builds) stays ignored.
**/kafka-sink-worker
!**/cmd/kafka-sink-worker/
!**/cmd/kafka-sink-worker/**

# Untracked local connector cruft — public/api/ holds locally-generated connector
# dirs with no tracked files; they show up in find/ls as "connectors" that don't
# exist in the repo. (public/database/ IS tracked — do not ignore it.)
shared/mcp-connectors/public/api/
# IDE
.cursor/
.cursorignore

# Editor swap & backup files (vim, emacs, etc.)
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Per-developer agent config and worktree metadata — should never be committed.
# The worktree dirs are created when devs run `git worktree add` under Claude
# Code or Claire (different sessions can each spawn one), and the untracked dirs
# were polluting `git status` across the repo.
#
# `.claude/` is ignored WHOLE, not just its worktrees: it is per-developer agent
# scratch (plans, PRDs, a permissions allowlist, LAN-specific proxy scripts), it
# is entry 7 of scripts/flip/excludes.txt so the public cut drops it anyway, and
# without this line the 14 files untracked alongside this change would be silently
# re-added by the next `git add -A`.
.claude/
.claire/worktrees/
backend-orchestrator/orchestrator
.env.staging

# Security-audit scanner OUTPUT (scripts/security-audit.sh). Raw machine-
# generated JSON/SARIF dumps (osv/govulncheck/trivy/bandit/gosec/…) run to
# ~185k lines and are regenerated on every run — artifacts, not source.
# The human-readable REPORT.md is kept (negated below) so the audit summary
# stays reviewable in git.
security-audit-results/*.json
security-audit-results/*.sarif
security-audit-results/_log_*.txt
security-audit-results/*.txt
!security-audit-results/REPORT.md
